  "name": "A Preliminary Look at Marine Mammal-food Chain Relationships in Alaskan Waters",
  "description": "This report proposes simplified food chains for three of the four broad areas of marine waters surrounding Alaska; allocates estimated total pinniped populations and biomass among the three areas; and, relates in some detail the proposed food chain to Northern fur seals. Because so little is known about the status and distribution of Cetaceans in Alaskan waters, they are not directly considered in this report,. [Reference: Sanger, Gerald A. A Preliminary Look at Marine Mammal-food Chain Relationships in Alaskan Waters. Marine Mammal Division, Northwest Fisheries Center, National Marine Fisheries Service, National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration, 17 May 1974.] Reprint available at the NOAA Seattle NMML Library.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: A report of collected data on a preliminary look at Marine mammal-food chain relationships in Alaskan waters.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563761",
